      {
        name: "move_robot",
        description: "Relocate one robot's base to a new pose in world, keeping its joint configuration. `robot` is the instance name the engine reports in get_robots_list; an engine hosting several moves that one and leaves the rest standing. A target with no orientation keeps the heading the base has. The move is refused with `resource_unavailable` for a robot that does not stand in the world, and with `rejected` for a target the implementer does not take. An orientation that turns by more than 1e-9 rad about an axis other than +z is refused with `rejected`, the message naming the part and what to send: an orientation [0, 0, sin(yaw/2), cos(yaw/2)]. An orientation whose squared norm lies 0.01 or more from 1 is refused with `rejected`, the tolerance of tf2's buffer that transforms names; the implementer normalizes each orientation it takes. It fails with `precondition_failed` when the placement rules that the contract description names refuse the place. The action gives no feedback and an empty result.",
        goal_service: {
          request_message_format: {
            robot: "string",
